# Here, There and Everywhere, verse (figure 96.2)
# Bars 2 and 4: Pollack types the C only in the second half of the bar, the first half left blank;
# read as the G held from the bar before. The C is also VI of e, the key the second line visits.
key G

system
chords              | G{I} | - C{IV} | G{I} | - C{IV / e: VI} |

system
chords              | f#{e: ii*} B{V} | f#{ii*} B{V} | e{e: i / G: vi} a{ii} | C{IV} D{V} |
caption * the f# chord is a "half-diminished" seventh: a diminished triad (F# A C) with a minor seventh (E)
